# Platform Terminology In FTL

- Use canonical platform terms in FTL for category/platform/domain wording instead of hardcoded UI copy.
- Prefer term references like `{ -platform-domain-create.label }`, `{ -platform-domain-business.label-plural }`, `{ -platform-domain-workplace.inline }`, and `{ -platform-ai-agent-product.label }`.
- Keep product names hardcoded when they are actual product names, for example `EveryAI`, `EveryBox`, `Enterprise Agent Studio`, `Screen Builder`, and `Flow Designer`.
- Do not invent new near-duplicate wording when an existing platform term already matches the intent.
- When a message needs app code access through `t('...')`, add a normal message key that references the term instead of duplicating the label text.

## Preferred Terms

- Create / AI Builder category: `-platform-domain-create`
- Business Domains / Business Suite category: `-platform-domain-business`
- EVERY workplace category: `-platform-domain-workplace`
- Enterprise agent worker wording: `-platform-ai-agent-product`

## Examples

```ftl
# ✅ GOOD
hero-title = { -platform-domain-business.label-plural }
tool-category = { -platform-domain-workplace.label }
task-step-type-ai-task-expert-description = { -platform-ai-agent-product.label } prompt step.

# ❌ BAD
hero-title = BUSINESS DOMAINS
tool-category = EVERY
task-step-type-ai-task-expert-description = Enterprise Agent prompt step.
```
